  "details": "The following stacktrace is appearing when transitioning to/from play mode:\n\n```\n\nInvalidOperationException: The NativeArray has been deallocated, it is not allowed to access it\n\nUnity.Collections.LowLevel.Unsafe.AtomicSafetyHandle.CheckReadAndThrowNoEarlyOut (Unity.Collections.LowLevel.Unsafe.AtomicSafetyHandle handle) (at <7d87237cea3743d093e22c5b98f74fba>:0)\n\nUnity.Collections.LowLevel.Unsafe.AtomicSafetyHandle.CheckReadAndThrow (Unity.Collections.LowLevel.Unsafe.AtomicSafetyHandle handle) (at <7d87237cea3743d093e22c5b98f74fba>:0)\n\nVRC.Collections.NativeList`1[T].get_Length () (at <13d2cdefdfcb463da789944b56f275ec>:0)\n\nVRC.Dynamics.ContactManager.RemoveContact (VRC.Dynamics.ContactBase contact) (at <3894c29d116744aab228d563a42e65b7>:0)\n\nVRC.Dynamics.ContactBase.OnDisable () (at <3894c29d116744aab228d563a42e65b7>:0)\n\nVRC.Dynamics.ContactReceiver.OnDisable () (at <3894c29d116744aab228d563a42e65b7>:0)\n\n```\n\nNote that this project creates and destroys PhysBones from within Awake callbacks (as part of Modular Avatar processing).",
